# hang.walk (order 1540): open an unread chat fifty times, each time with
# the flash owed a write while the UI core folds the page. The window the
# M9 hung in on 2026-11-07 (1534: core 0 writes or erases the flash while
# core 1 is parked inside the critical section it allocates under) is
# re-armed before every open, so the race is under load every time, not
# only on the first open as in window 10.
#
# Each block is Lew's case: a message arrives in "Bench", the bench's own
# conversation (1562: never a real chat; the board selects it), the owe is
# armed, Enter opens it: the read mark goes to the ring (never to the
# home) and every row to the summary log while core 1 folds and
# allocates. The walk opens chats, so it runs only on a board joined to
# the bench home (scripts/m9-bench-home.sh). Even
# blocks close both stores' sectors first, so the writes erase (about 45
# ms with core 0's interrupts off, after which the keyboard's 10 ms tick
# is always pending); odd blocks only write.
#
# Run it on the diagnosis image (the fix 04b20b78 reverted, built with
# --bench): expected FAIL with a [PREV_RUN] reason=wdt0|wdt1 line. Then on
# the fix image: expected PASS, fifty [OPEN] lines, no [PREV_RUN] with a
# record.
#
#   just m9-walk <rig> scripts/m9-walks/hang.walk <bench elf>
#
# The bars are 1533's except the key bar: Enter on a long chat took up to
# 1.7 s in window 10 and the median key 170 ms, which is 1507's to fix and
# the [OPEN] lines' to explain; this walk asks whether the board hangs.
#
# The closing `idle` holds the board's key counts to the walk (1612): the
# last [UART] line's keys_rx= equals the key frames sent since the boot (a
# frame lost on the line fails by name, as window 23's Back at block 21
# was) and keys_ui= is no less (a press no UI turn read). After a lost
# Back the next block's Enter lands in the open chat; since 1612 it opens
# nothing the M9 does not draw, so the walk is back in step one block
# later instead of standing on the chat to its end.
allow key_ms 2000

# open 1 of 50
bench arrive
bench owe erase
key enter
wait page=chat
key back
wait page=chats

# open 2 of 50
bench arrive
bench owe
key enter
wait page=chat
key back
wait page=chats

# open 3 of 50
bench arrive
bench owe erase
key enter
wait page=chat
key back
wait page=chats

